        "id": "maxim:microbiology:bacterial-biology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "microbiology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[bacterial, biology]",
        "section": "microbiology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Bacterial Biology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GRAM-NEGATIVE EXTRAS:\n  ─ Outer membrane: Phospholipid bilayer, asymmetric\n  ─ LPS (lipopolysaccharide):\n    Lipid A: Embedded in outer leaflet → TLR4 agonist → endotoxin\n    Core: Conserved oligosaccharide\n    O-antigen: Highly variable polysaccharide → bacterial serotyping\n  ─ Porins: β-barrel channels in outer membrane (passive transport)\n  ─ Periplasmic space: Between inner and outer membranes\n    Contains: β-lactamases (destroy penicillins), drug efflux proteins"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-BACTERIAL-BIOLOGY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "01-BACTERIAL-BIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
