        "section": "microbiology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Bacterial Biology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ANTIBIOTIC TARGETS IN CELL WALL:\n  β-lactam antibiotics: Block penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs)\n    → PBPs are transpeptidases that cross-link peptidoglycan\n    → Weakened cell wall → osmotic lysis\n  Vancomycin: Binds D-Ala-D-Ala terminus of peptide bridge\n    → Blocks transpeptidase substrate access\n  Polymyxins: Disrupt outer membrane (gram-negative specific)"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-BACTERIAL-BIOLOGY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "01-BACTERIAL-BIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
